Default methods vs static methods in java 8
---------------------------------------------
Feature                can be overridden by implementing class       How to call the method
Default                 Yes                                           On an Object of the implementing class
Static                  No                                            Using the interface name

use cases:
----------
  Default:Provide common functionality for most implementations of the interface
  Static:Define utility methods that dont depend on the state of an object.provide helper methods for other interface methods

Why were default and static methods introduced ?
------------------------------------------------
->Backward compatibility
->improved interface functionality
Overall ,default and static methods make interfaces more powerful and flexible,enabling them to evolve overtime without breaking existing code and offering additional functionality to improve code maintainability.


